This code is adapted from Dunipace et.al, Genetics, 2025 to quantify in-situ intensity and width of brk signal for over 10+ embryos. 
See Dunipace et.al, Genetics, 2025 for additional information regarding the custom LUT. 

In order to quantify the images, the first command to utilize is: 
[im_{name}, data_{name}] = quantify_in_situ;

In order to visualize what was quantified, use the following command: 
display_mask_3D(im_{name}, data_{name});
Toggle display mask to see the segmented region




The following visualization GUI will popped up for visual inspection of segmented. 

Once image is quantified, thresholds can be change to appropriately measure the RNA structure of interests: 
for i = 1:44

data(i).T_bg_avg = 0.03;

data(i).T_sig_avg = 0.008;

end

In which T_bg_avg is threshold for background and T_sig_avg is threshold for detected segmented structure signal 

Once everything looks perfectly segmented. Plots can be made using the following command: 
[stat, p, p_ttest, avg, stat_all, p_all, mean_y, err_y, groups]...
= plot_in_situ_quantification(data_{name},...
'norm_I_avg', [1,2,3,4], [1:4], false, {'variable_name'}, false,...
[], {'variable_name'}, false);
